      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Turn timeout does not cover runtime initialization",
      "description": "The timeout explicitly wraps only `thread.run`, but runtime startup, `initialize`, and `thread_start` precede it. A hung startup therefore bypasses the cap, contradicting line 82\u2019s claim that startup hangs are bounded. Extend the deadline to cover initialization and thread creation, and specify bounded cleanup when initialization stalls.",
