    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Interactive authentication has unbounded I/O paths",
      "description": "The login deadline covers only `handle.wait()`. Runtime startup and the initial browser/device-code login RPC occur before it; logout has no specified deadline. Cancellation also awaits `handle.cancel()` without describing what happens when the runtime is unresponsive or disconnects mid-request.\n\nDefine deadlines and explicit disconnect/error handling for login initiation, logout, and cancellation, including subprocess cleanup when graceful cancellation fails. Otherwise the new authentication commands can hang despite the design\u2019s stated timeout handling.",
